# PHASE 2 — Orders and billing

**Goal:** the portal replaces the paper order book. This is the most valuable phase.

### 2.1 Order model

Orders with embedded items exactly as specified in CLAUDE.md, plus `orderNo`
generation in `YYYY-NNNN` form, sequential per year and safe under concurrent
creation. Zod schemas. Tests for the number generator.

**Checkpoint — stop and report.**

### 2.2 Order creation flow (no images yet)

`/orders/new`:

1. Pick a customer by phone search, or create one inline
2. Add one or more items. Per item: garment type (rate auto-fills, editable for
   this order), quantity, measurements (reuse the customer's latest set for that
   garment type or take a new one inline with `MeasurementForm`), cloth source
   (customer-brought or shop-provided), free-text note, due date
3. Running bill panel updating live as items change
4. Discount and advance payment fields
5. Save as draft

Snapshot `garmentTypeName` and `rate` onto each item at save time — changing the
rate card later must never alter a past order's price.

**Checkpoint — stop and report.**

### 2.3 Images

Signed Cloudinary uploads, signature generated server-side, API secret never
reaching the browser. Per item: cloth photo, reference image, pattern image,
multiple of each kind. Camera or gallery, multiple at once, upload progress,
remove before save. Store `url`, `publicId`, `kind`. Display via Cloudinary
transforms — thumbnails in grids, larger on tap, never the original file in a list.
Handle oversized files, wrong types, and going offline mid-upload.

**Checkpoint — stop and report.**

### 2.4 Order listing, detail, and status

- `/orders` — filters by status and due-date range, sorted by soonest due date.
  Row shows order no, customer, item count, total, balance, promised date, status.
- `/orders/[id]` — items as cards with photos, measurements used, notes, due date,
  per-item status; bill summary; edit and status actions.
- `lib/orders/transition.ts` — the single place any status changes. Validates the
  transition is legal, records who and when, and derives the parent order status
  from item statuses. No `order.status = …` anywhere else in the codebase.

**Checkpoint — stop and report.**

### 2.5 Invoice PDF

`@react-pdf/renderer`, must run on Vercel's serverless runtime with no headless
browser. Shop header, order number and date, customer name and phone, line items
(garment, qty, rate, amount), subtotal, discount, total, advance, balance, due
dates. Served from `/api/orders/[id]/invoice` as `application/pdf`, with a
download button on the order page.

**Phase 2 acceptance:** I can take a complete multi-item order with photos and
measurements, see the bill calculate correctly, and download a clean invoice.

