# PHASE 3 — Confirmation flow

**Goal:** customers confirm orders over WhatsApp, with no dependency on Meta.

Read CLAUDE.md section 7 carefully. This phase is about the abstraction as much as
the feature — if the boundary is wrong here, Phase 5 becomes a rewrite.

### 3.1 Messaging abstraction

`lib/messaging/` exporting the `MessagingProvider` interface from CLAUDE.md, plus
`providers/manual.ts` which composes a plain-text WhatsApp message (shop contact
details, each item with garment / qty / rate / due date, bill totals, link to the
public order page) and returns a `wa.me` URL. Provider chosen by the
`MESSAGING_PROVIDER` env var, defaulting to manual.

No code outside `lib/messaging/` may reference `wa.me`, Meta, or templates.
**Show me the interface signatures before implementing.**

**Checkpoint — stop and report.**

### 3.2 Public order page

`/o/[token]` — no authentication, access by a cryptographically random 32-character
token stored on the order. The order `_id` never appears in the URL.

Read-only, mobile-first: shop header, customer name, each item with cloth and
reference photos, notes, due date, prices, totals, advance, balance. Two buttons —
"Confirm this order" records the confirmation server-side and thanks them;
"I'd like a change" shows the shop's phone number. Tokens are generated when the
order is first sent and invalidated on delivery or cancellation.

**Checkpoint — stop and report.**

### 3.3 Wiring it up

- "Send for confirmation" on a draft: generates the token, moves the order to
  `awaiting_confirmation`, opens the `wa.me` link with the message prefilled
- Confirmation state shown on the order: sent at, viewed at, confirmed at
- Manual "Mark as confirmed" for customers who reply in chat instead of tapping,
  recording which staff member marked it
- On confirmation: customer `lead` → `active`, order → `confirmed`
- Everything goes through `lib/orders/transition.ts`

**Phase 3 acceptance:** I can send an order for confirmation from my phone, open
the link as a customer, confirm it, and watch the status change in the portal.

